    <h1>GPT-3: Generative Pre-trained Transformer 3</h1>
    <p>GPT-3 is a large-scale language model created by OpenAI. It was one of the first models to show that "scaling up" leads to significantly better performance on a wide variety of NLP tasks without any specific fine-tuning.</p>
    
    <h2>Scale and Capacity</h2>
    <p>With 175 billion parameters, GPT-3 was an order of magnitude larger than its predecessor, GPT-2. It was trained on hundreds of gigabytes of text data from various sources including Common Crawl, WebText2, and Wikipedia.</p>
    
    <h2>Zero-shot, One-shot, and Few-shot Learning</h2>
    <p>GPT-3 is particularly famous for its ability to perform tasks it wasn't explicitly trained for, simply by providing it with a prompt. For example, you can give it a few examples of English-to-French translation, and it will pick up the pattern and translate the next sentence correctly.</p>

    <p>Try searching for "OpenAI" or "Few-shot" in the agent!</p>
